license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A reproducible computational study of when calibrated AI confidence warrants
  reliance: decision costs and deferral, finite-sample uncertainty in reliability
  evidence, distribution shift and recalibration, and subgroup burdens under
  limited human review. Uses UCI credit-card default and ACSIncome data.
